 ('4.1 Cross-domain interaction', 'P', 'drill.js XD, claims.js ckOpen, entity.js enXd', 'Added 21 Nov in 14.0: six tested links compare your own logged days with and without a cause: sleep to dials, sleep to BAC, late bedtime to BAC, BAC day to dials, training to next-day dials, money day to dials. Each needs 5 days on each side, gives both averages and the day counts, and says it is a pattern, not proof. Shown on the kinds-of-number page, the dials and BAC metric pages, and on records about those areas. Correction 21 Nov: the Money screen already had a runway in days (money2.js, spendable cash ÷ 30-day spending), so the earlier note saying there was none was wrong. 14.7 replaced it with an honest one (see the planner row). A money day → runway link was not added: runway is one figure for the whole period, not something each day has, so a with-and-without-days comparison has nothing to compare; the runway page instead shows recorded income a month against spending a month. Still missing: tennis lessons as their own record, and links feeding the plan; mcBuild does not use them.'),
 ('5 Learning without questionnaires', 'P', 'Log anything, ask.js, calendar, Todoist, Sheet sync', 'No passive sources beyond those.'),
 ('6 Hardware and sensing', 'N', '', 'Your direction of 21 Nov: one personal device, perhaps a watch, that does everything and is built around you, after everything else is finished. A research document, no purchase. Not started.'),
 ('7 World intelligence', 'P', 'content library, daily scan, sources that disagree', 'No world-model validation; server search has no quota.', 'sdxOpen'),
 ('8 Knowledge graph and causal hypotheses', 'P', 'intel.js (experiments), entity.js, link kinds', 'CHECKED LINE BY LINE 21 Nov. An experiment kept baseline, hypothesis, the one change, the comparison, the result and the decision. Missing were other explanations, what else changed, how sure you are, and the follow-up; added in 13.77, and a conclusion without the first two is marked provisional. The app does not propose competing explanations itself.'),
 ('9 Limits of its own knowledge', 'P', 'claims.js, minimum-evidence rules in model.js, fidelity.js, forecast.js', 'CHECKED LINE BY LINE 21 Nov. The six kinds of uncertainty are now named on the kinds-of-number page, each with what the app really does about it (13.77). Added 21 Nov in 13.99: every scorecard number now carries its own How sure line: counts say what they cannot include, typed figures say nobody checked them, answer and owner rates show a likely range (90%) and the number of dials under them, and fewer than 30 dials is called too few to rely on. Still not attached: numbers outside the scorecard (money totals, forecasts, the funnel model).', 'ckOpen'),
 ('10 Future Lab simulation', 'P', 'future.js, scenarios', 'No simulation with ranges. Your decision of 21 Nov: it starts when everything else is finished; it also waits until forecasts have a track record.'),
 ('11 Prediction, backtesting, calibration', 'B', 'judge.js, forecast.js', 'Read in full 21 Nov. A forecast records the variable, the week, a range and a middle value, the method and its version, how many weeks it rests on, and the actual result. Three variables; the first real marked week comes after Monday 23 Nov. Scoring rules for probabilities are not used.', 'fctOpen'),
 ('12 Decisions and experiments', 'B', 'judge.js, intel.js', 'CHECKED LINE BY LINE 21 Nov. A decision kept twelve of the sixteen parts the addendum lists. Added in 13.78: which objective it serves, the constraints, what you give up by choosing it, and a trigger to revisit it sooner. The owner of every decision is you, so there is no field for it. Expected value and sensitivity are not calculated.', 'jlOpen'),
